course: dictionary
lesson: 1300
title: What is a byte?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A byte is a small unit that computers use to store information. It is made of 8 bits, and each bit is a single one or zero. «One byte can store one letter like A», so a short word takes up several bytes. Think of a byte as one tiny box that holds one letter.
explain: Eight bits make a byte, and 8 bits can make 256 different patterns, the numbers 0 to 255. «That is why colour values often go from 0 to 255.» Each pattern is a different number the computer can hold.
explain: Bytes measure how big things are. A photo, a song or a game takes up a certain number of bytes, and we count them in bigger groups: kilobytes (KB), megabytes (MB), gigabytes (GB) and terabytes (TB). If a file is 2 MB, it takes up about two million bytes of space.
fact: A byte is a unit of computer memory or data.
fact: A byte is a group of 8 bits, and a bit is a single one or zero.
fact: One byte can store one letter, such as «A».
fact: Eight bits make 256 patterns, the numbers 0 to 255.
fact: Kilobytes, megabytes, gigabytes and terabytes are bigger groups of bytes, used to measure file sizes.
exercise: What is a byte made of? | One megabyte | *Eight bits | Eight songs | Ten words
exercise: «One byte can store one letter like A.» How many letters can one byte store? | A whole page | Two | *One | Eight
exercise: Which unit is the biggest? | Byte | Kilobyte | *Terabyte | Bit
test: «Eight bits make a byte, which can hold 256 patterns.» How many patterns can 8 bits make? | 8 | 0 | *256 | 1000
test: Why do we measure a photo or game in bytes? | *To show how much space it takes up | To show who made the file | To change the colour of the picture | To make the file glow
exam: «An overflow is a bug where a number gets too big for the space it is stored in.» In one byte, what is 255 plus 1? | 256 | *0 | 255 | 1
